========================================================================
  OVERALL FINDINGS TABLE
========================================================================
  saved table: Table_FINDINGS_overall_v9.csv
  - Sector concentration hypothesis (former H4)
      finding: REJECTED. Standalone per-sector FE: 2/13 significant at 5%; predicted-strong (semis, apparel) not significant.
      => Report as robustness, not a core hypothesis.
  - Semiconductors (the v8 centrepiece)
      finding: beta=-0.0197, p=0.36 (NOT significant); 80% US.
      => v8 result (beta=-0.179 on 6 firms) does not replicate on 15 firms.
  - Sectors significant at 5% (standalone FE)
      finding: Medical Devices (b=-0.033, p=0.046), Consumer Staples (b=-0.032, p=0.027)
      => Signal concentrated in a few NON-predicted sectors, not apparel/semis.
  - Borderline sectors (5-10%)
      finding: Mass Retail (p=0.058), Bldg Materials (p=0.058)
      => Mass Retail sits here (p~0.06): treat as suggestive, NOT significant.
  - Method note: interaction vs standalone
      finding: Interaction model uses Staples as reference, so Staples cannot appear in its significant set; standalone FE shows Staples IS significant.
      => Significant-sector identity is method-dependent; standalone FE is the reported basis.
  - US dominance of significant sectors
      finding: Significant sectors are US-heavy (Med Devices 71%, semis 80%).
      => Disclose: sector results lean on US firms; not a global claim.
  - US-only vs international (Table 21)
      finding: Per-sector slopes broadly similar in sign; most insignificant in both cuts.
      => No sector shows a robust international-specific concentration.
  - Same-year DCFO interaction (Table 23)
      finding: Cash channel more broadly negative across sectors (semis beta=-0.199).
      => Consistent with H2 breadth; not a revival of sector-H4.
  - Small-multiples (Figure, all 13 sectors)
      finding: Most sectors gentle negative-insignificant; significant at 5%: Medical Devices (b=-0.033, p=0.046), Consumer Staples (b=-0.032, p=0.027).
      => Single exhibit answers "why these sectors" - broad, modest, not concentrated.

